{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Operator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13)\n'One source of contention for CI runners in this project is the reconciler bridge job and canary. let's double the time between runs for both jobs and for both fallback and the chained reconciler invocation.'\n\n## Context / Problem\nRunner-contention analysis (dotted-uncheery-dunnart / sunbear AC2) found 609 `workflow_dispatch` runs on main in ~33h starving the Verified lane; the reconcile-bridge self-rescheduling chain is the dominant dispatch source. Every bridge/canary cadence must halve in frequency.\n\n## Approach\nFour cadence levers, all doubled:\n\n1. **Bridge cron backstop** — `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` `schedule:` goes from the single entry `*/20 * * * *` to a **uniform 40-minute** cadence. Cron cannot express 40 minutes in one entry, so use the three-entry 2-hour cycle GitHub Actions accepts under one `schedule:` key: `0 0-23/2 * * *`, `40 0-23/2 * * *`, `20 1-23/2 * * *` (fires :00, :40, 1:20, 2:00, … — gaps uniformly 40 min).\n2. **Chain pacing** — the re-dispatch step (\"Re-dispatch to sustain the continuous loop (opt-in)\") calls `gh workflow run` immediately, so the chain's inter-invocation period equals exactly **one** pass duration (~7 min here, per `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`). There is no existing delay knob. Introduce one that is self-tuning rather than a repo-specific literal, since this file is a client-copied TEMPLATE: a new early step records `PASS_STARTED_EPOCH` into `$GITHUB_ENV`, and the re-dispatch step sleeps for the pass's own elapsed duration before dispatching. Period becomes **two** pass durations — literally doubled at any pass duration, for any adopter. Bounded twice so pacing can never convert a slow pass into a `timeout-minutes: 60` kill: the sleep is capped by repo Variable `RECONCILE_CHAIN_PACING_CAP_MINUTES` (default **15**), and is skipped outright once elapsed >= 30 min (such a pass already paces itself and the remaining job budget must stay free). Pacing is inside the existing `if: !cancelled() && vars.RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS == 'true'` gate, so template default (chain off) is unaffected.\n3. **Canary schedule** — `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` `0 * * * *` (hourly) -> `0 */2 * * *` (2-hourly).\n4. **Canary staleness window** — the canary's own header states the window rationale as \"3x cadence\"; at a 40-min cadence that floor rises 1h -> 2h, which equals today's default window, so leaving it would make the canary alarm on healthy-but-late runs. Double the default `ALERT_WINDOW_HOURS` 2 -> 4 (workflow `env:` default and the `alert_window_hours` input default/description), preserving the same 2x margin over the floor. `scripts/canary_bridge.py` reads the value from the environment and has no hard-coded default, so no code default changes; only its ticket-body string \"(cron: */20)\" needs to stop naming the retired literal.\n\n**Jenkins parity.** `Jenkinsfile` carries the same backstop as `cron('H/20 * * * *')`. Jenkins `H/40` yields non-uniform 40/20 gaps, so mirror the GitHub three-entry 2-hour cycle in the multi-line form `cron('''0 0-23/2 * * *\\n40 0-23/2 * * *\\n20 1-23/2 * * *''')`. `.gitlab-ci.yml` carries no cron (GitLab schedules are configured server-side) and needs no edit.\n\n**Truthfulness.** Every comment naming `*/20` or \"hourly\" is rewritten to the new numbers: `reconcile-bridge.yml` header lines ~20-23 and re-dispatch comments/`::warning::` text; canary header staleness paragraph; `scripts/canary_bridge.py` alert body; `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` cadence table, the \"Continuous loop — running more often than the 20-minute floor\" heading (plus its three in-repo anchor links) and its bullets; the exit-75 row naming \"the next */20 run\"; `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py` docstring.\n\n**Latency note.** Worst-case reconcile latency doubles (20 -> 40 min backstop) and canary detection latency doubles (1h -> 2h poll, 2h -> 4h window). Recorded in `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` alongside the cadence table — that table is the authoritative cadence home. `docs/ci-provider-matrix.md` is about the external LLM suite's provider cadence, not the bridge, so it is deliberately not touched.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` — schedule entries, new pass-start step, paced re-dispatch, comment rewrites.\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` — schedule, `ALERT_WINDOW_HOURS` default + input default/description, header rationale.\n- `Jenkinsfile` — mirrored 40-minute backstop.\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py` — alert-body cadence string.\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` — cadence table, continuous-loop section + heading + anchors, latency note.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py` — `_UNCHANGED_CRONS[\"reconcile-bridge.yml\"]`.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py` — `test_reconcilers_keep_their_own_schedules_and_never_cancel`.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py` — `test_github_schedule_and_continuous_redispatch_remain_compatible`.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py` — docstring + re-dispatch harness if the paced step changes its shell contract.\n\n## Testing\n- **Happy path:** the three cadence-pinning tests above assert the new literals — `_UNCHANGED_CRONS` and `test_reconcilers_keep_their_own_schedules_and_never_cancel` compare the full three-entry list, `test_github_schedule_and_continuous_redispatch_remain_compatible` compares `workflow[True][\"schedule\"]` to the three-dict list.\n- **Uniformity:** a new assertion in `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py` derives the fire times of the bridge's three cron entries over one 2-hour cycle and asserts every consecutive gap is exactly 40 minutes — this is the property the three-entry spelling exists to satisfy, and a literal-only pin would not catch a future edit that keeps three entries but breaks uniformity.\n- **Edge / failure path:** extend the existing `_run_redispatch` harness in `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py` so the paced step is exercised with (a) a short elapsed time (sleep taken, capped value not hit) and (b) an elapsed time past the 30-minute skip threshold (no sleep, dispatch still issued) — with the sleep stubbed on `PATH` so the test records the requested duration instead of waiting. The existing disabled-workflow-422 benign-no-op test must still pass unchanged.\n- **Gates:** `make lint`, `make typecheck`, actionlint/zizmor workflow gates, and the full CI unit selection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` `schedule:` holds exactly the three entries `0 0-23/2 * * *`, `40 0-23/2 * * *`, `20 1-23/2 * * *`, and a test asserts consecutive fire-time gaps are uniformly 40 minutes.\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` schedule is `0 */2 * * *` and its `ALERT_WINDOW_HOURS` default (env + input) is `4`.\n- [ ] The re-dispatch step sleeps for the pass's own elapsed duration before dispatching, capped by `RECONCILE_CHAIN_PACING_CAP_MINUTES` (default 15) and skipped above 30 minutes elapsed; a test asserts both the sleeping and the skipping branch.\n- [ ] `Jenkinsfile` carries the same three-entry 40-minute backstop.\n- [ ] `grep -rn '\\*/20' .github/workflows/ Jenkinsfile scripts/ docs/jira-sync-setup.md` returns no hits, and no comment or doc still says the canary is \"hourly\" or the window is 2h.\n- [ ] The four cadence-pinning tests named in Scope pass against the new literals, and `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the CI unit selection are green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786614388900428001,"uuid":"1adf5b69-7ff9-4aa9-97bb-d38a290210ac"}